Hacker Clicker Privacy Policy
Effective October 4, 2026
Hacker Clicker is a single-player game made by Range Ban. This policy explains what the game does with information about you. The short version: we don't collect anything ourselves; the ads in the free version are served by Google, which does.
What we collect. Nothing. The game has no accounts, no sign-in and no analytics of its own. We never see your name, email, contacts, location or device identifiers.
Your save data. Your progress, settings and achievements are stored only on your device. If you use the in-game backup feature, the code it shows you is yours to copy and keep; it is never sent to us. Uninstalling the game or clearing its data deletes your save.
Checking the time. To stop changed phone clocks from faking idle earnings and daily rewards, the game asks a public server (Google, Apple or Cloudflare) for the current time when it opens. This is a plain HTTPS request with no information about you. Like any internet request, it reveals your IP address to that server, under that company's own privacy policy. We receive nothing.
Purchases. The optional in-app purchase is processed by Google Play under Google's privacy policy. We do not receive your payment details; the game only learns whether the purchase was made so it can unlock it.
Advertising. The free version shows ads served by Google AdMob, including an optional rewarded ad you choose to watch. To show and measure ads, Google may collect your device's advertising ID, your approximate location from your IP address, and how you interact with ads, under Google's privacy policy. Where the law requires it, the game asks for your consent before showing personalized ads. You can reset your advertising ID or opt out of personalized ads in your Android settings. Buying the Lawyer removes ads for good.
Children. The game is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from anyone.
Changes. If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new effective date.
Contact. Questions: rangebanned@gmail.com.
